Normative-document review (round 1). A NEW document was drafted today and is intended to become the project's standing SPEC for future modifications: docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md ("研究边界与修改指导方略" — Research Boundary & Modification Guide, 2026-09-29).

What the document claims to be: the convergence of the LMABO (arXiv:2602.07904, ICLR 2026) reading round and the architecture discussions into a normative spec. It contains: (0) one-page decision card; (1) abstract reference architecture (5 layers: exogenous / state / policy / execution / output; two-level decision structure with episode boundary, SMDP/options semantics; mapping to agent-harness vocabulary); (2) component taxonomy — A-class definitional-frozen, B-class in-episode adjustable (B1 theory-backed / B2 empirically established / B3 thin-literature), C-class forbidden in-episode and externalized to the meta level, plus a classification of the project's 8 ActionTypes; (3) formalized research boundary — frozen set as minimal invariants of measurability, two meanings of "measurability" (adaptedness vs per-decision supervision), what C-class actions lose (statability/attributability/comparability), and a "three-gate check" for any new action slot; (4) interface contracts (meta-actions only at episode boundaries, warm start across episodes, meta level = bandit over configurations, P2/P3 reuse at both levels, harness version freeze); (5) expected outcomes (capability / science / theory goals + testable success criteria); (6) modification procedures (new action slot, new state features, model-change impulse mapping table, multi-objective extension, LLM-introduction discipline); (7) literature anchors; (8) open problems; (9) glossary. Normative modal words are defined: 必须 (must) / 禁止 (forbidden) / 允许 (allowed) / 建议 (recommended).

The document's intended role going forward: it governs WHAT may be modified in this codebase and WHAT checks a modification must pass BEFORE it is legal. Violations of 禁止 rules are declared to invalidate produced data/conclusions. So this review's stakes are higher than a paper draft: errors here become false constraints or false permissions for months.

