C. Theoretical soundness of the NEW normative claims (not just accuracy): the C-class argument (mid-episode kernel/posterior/surrogate change destroys theorem statability rather than performance); the "legal neighbors" distinctions (amortized inference / design-phase kernel choice / SMAC mirror); the warm-start contract (§4.2 — is "定理按以初始数据为条件照常适用" stated with the right caveats?); the meta level as bandit over configurations with independent regret theory; the multi-objective "swap two plugins" claim; anything in §3 (frozen set = minimal invariants; the two measurability layers; the three-gate check) that is wrong, vacuous, or unenforceable as written.

