their rank drops to as low as 35th, highlighting the risk of a fixed strategy. In addition, adaptive
portfolio methods, though achieving competitive results, frequently exhibit higher variability and
are less robust across the heterogeneous problem suite. These approaches depend on heuristics for
weighting past acquisition performance and thus can be slow to adapt when the task-specific land-


